      "sourceTextSha256": "c1f1c0de022c3513d15c0c1375dab8980b645551fc49c611a1d4c78670d025c0",
      "text": "Day 8 · Granada, one of the oldest colonial cities on the American mainland, founded in 1524, has survived pirate attacks, civil wars and fires. Visit the main square, the Casa de los Leones cultural centre, the San Francisco convent and museum, the Ceramics Museum, La Merced church and La Calzada. Then discover the culture and history of Nicaragua in Managua, its museums, parks and historic sites, and Masaya Volcano National Park, the country’s first national park, to see its active crater, followed by the famous Masaya craft market. Overnight at Hotel Real La Merced. (B)",
